-- | The closed set of administrative roles for the AccessControl layer.
--
-- Using a sum type (rather than free `Text`, as in EVM's `bytes32` role ids)
-- keeps role identifiers exhaustive, typo-proof, and lintable — see
-- docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §1 (correction C4). New roles are added here as the
-- registry grows; every consumer that pattern-matches on `Role` is then forced
-- by the compiler to handle the new case.
module SimpleToken.Admin.Roles where

-- | A single administrative capability a registry administrator can grant.
--
-- `Admin` is the root governance role — the OpenZeppelin `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE` /
-- `Ownable` owner analogue. A holder of an `Admin` capability may issue and
-- revoke other (non-`Admin`) capabilities (delegated governance), which is how
-- operational "ownership" is handed to a new party without reassigning the
-- immutable instrument admin party. See docs/ADMIN-LAYER-PLAN.md §5.
--
-- Enforcement status (what currently gates on each role):
--   * `Pauser` — enforced by `Rules_SetPaused`.
--   * `Admin`  — enforced by the `TokenAdministrator` delegated choices.
--   * `Minter` — enforced by `Rules_Mint` (AL-5); carries an optional D3 allowance.
--   * `Burner` — enforced by `SimpleHolding_ForcedBurn` (AL-6, clawback).
--   * `BatchProcessor` — RESERVED: defined so capabilities are mintable ahead of
--     the slice that consumes it (V2-10 delegated settlement). No choice gates on
--     it yet, so granting it authorizes nothing today. Do not treat it as live
--     access control until its slice lands.
data Role
  = Minter          -- ^ May create holdings via `Rules_Mint` (AL-5). Enforced; instrument-scopable.
  | Burner          -- ^ May force-burn holdings via `SimpleHolding_ForcedBurn` (AL-6). Enforced.
  | Pauser          -- ^ May flip the registry pause flag (see SimpleToken.Rules). Enforced.
  | BatchProcessor  -- ^ (reserved) Delegated SettlementFactory_SettleBatch — future slice (V2-10).
  | Admin           -- ^ Root governance: may issue/revoke capabilities (owner analogue). Enforced.
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | The role-admin relation (AL-8): which role administers each role — the
-- OpenZeppelin `getRoleAdmin` analogue, replacing the flat
-- `delegableRole : Role -> Bool` MVP policy. A holder of `roleAdmin R`
-- (registry-wide) may issue/revoke role `R` through the delegated
-- `TokenAdministrator` choices; the genesis root may still manage every role
-- directly. Used by BOTH the delegated-issue and delegated-revoke paths so the
-- hierarchy cannot drift between them (see SimpleToken.Admin.Authority).
--
-- TT-Q-008a — **compiled pure function, not runtime-mutable state.** Reconfiguring
-- the hierarchy (e.g. introducing a `MinterAdmin` distinct from the default admin)
-- is a deliberate package upgrade that edits a case below, NOT a live
-- `setRoleAdmin` transaction — so there is no `RoleAdminConfig` contract for every
-- gated grant to disclose, and exhaustiveness is preserved. The generic
-- `oz-access-control` side stays mechanism-only: its role-admin-aware grant/revoke
-- take the required admin role as a `Text` the consumer supplies, computed here
-- and mapped through `roleId` — so the library hard-codes no role graph.
--
-- TT-Q-008c — **flat default.** Every role's admin is `Admin` (the
-- `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE` analogue), so by default an `Admin` holder may delegate
-- every operational role — matching OZ `AccessControl` breadth and the
-- separation-of-duties US FIs expect. Intermediate admin roles are opt-in later.
--
--   * `Admin`'s admin is `Admin` (it self-administers in OZ). But re-delegating
--     root is **not** allowed through the delegated path: `SimpleToken.Admin.Authority`
--     refuses to issue/revoke `Admin` there (the `AccessControlDefaultAdminRules`
--     posture, preserving safety decision C9). `Admin` moves only via the genesis
--     root or the two-step + timelocked default-admin handoff.
--   * `Minter`/`Burner`/`BatchProcessor` are administered by `Admin`, so an `Admin`
--     delegate may now appoint them (broader than the old root-only policy). Point
--     a case at a narrower admin role to scope that authority.
--
-- The explicit per-constructor cases are deliberate (no wildcard): adding a new
-- `Role` forces a deliberate admin assignment here. The package builds with
-- `-Werror=incomplete-patterns` (see simple-token/daml.yaml), so a missing clause
-- is a compile error, not a runtime pattern-match crash.
roleAdmin : Role -> Role
roleAdmin Minter = Admin
roleAdmin Burner = Admin
roleAdmin Pauser = Admin
roleAdmin BatchProcessor = Admin
roleAdmin Admin = Admin

-- | The typed-wrapper bridge (AL-7): map this token's closed, exhaustive `Role`
-- sum to the `Text` role ids the generic `OpenZeppelin.AccessControl` library
-- uses (the `bytes32` analogue — a generic, monomorphic library cannot store a
-- closed sum; see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §5). The token keeps compile-time
-- exhaustiveness in its own API and only crosses to `Text` at the library
-- boundary in `SimpleToken.Admin.Capability.requireRole`. Per-constructor (no
-- wildcard) so a new `Role` must be given an id deliberately, enforced by
-- `-Werror=incomplete-patterns`.
roleId : Role -> Text
roleId Minter = "MINTER_ROLE"
roleId Burner = "BURNER_ROLE"
roleId Pauser = "PAUSER_ROLE"
roleId BatchProcessor = "BATCH_PROCESSOR_ROLE"
roleId Admin = "DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE"
